Global correctness: allocation-sale-price-derived-cost (run 2).
Sale prices do not determine acquisition basis. Assigning 800 USD of basis to
units acquired for 400 USD is impossible even if the sales eventually close
the position.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight unrealized-gains --to 2024-03-31 --format json <<'LEDGER'
commodity USD
  format 1,000.00 USD
  default
commodity FUND
  format 1,000.000 FUND
account Assets:Bank
account Assets:Broker
account Income:CapitalGains

P 2024-02-01 FUND 1000 USD
P 2024-03-01 FUND 50 USD

2024-01-01 First acquisition
  Assets:Broker  6 FUND {{600 USD}}
  Assets:Bank  -600 USD

2024-01-02 Second acquisition
  Assets:Broker  4 FUND {{400 USD}}
  Assets:Bank  -400 USD

2024-02-01 High-price sale
  Assets:Broker  -4 FUND {{800 USD}} @@ 4000 USD
  Assets:Bank  4000 USD
  Income:CapitalGains  -3200 USD

2024-03-01 Low-price sale
  Assets:Broker  -3 FUND {{100 USD}} @@ 150 USD
  Assets:Bank  150 USD
  Income:CapitalGains  -50 USD

2024-04-01 Final sale
  Assets:Broker  -3 FUND {{100 USD}} @@ 900 USD
  Assets:Bank  900 USD
  Income:CapitalGains  -800 USD
LEDGER

========== OUTPUT ==========

[
  {
    "account": "Assets:Broker",
    "quantity": "50",
    "commodity": "USD"
  }
]

========== WARNINGS ==========

[IMPOSSIBLE_COST_BASIS] High-price sale: Assets:Broker sold 4 FUND with cost 800 USD; allowed range is 400 to 400 USD
  <stdin>:22:3
